{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552330-spirit-magic-paradigm-vs-reality","id":1552330,"title":"Spirit magic paradigm vs reality","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2025-07-13T07:21:24-07:00","id":1552330,"title":"Spirit magic paradigm vs reality","content":"A shaman may have a paradigm that all magic comes from spirit pacts. Not all effects are spirits though in reality. A healing life effect can be implemented for example without a spirit and the casting mage only believes it does. But here we have the problem how would said mage rationalise his made believe spirits vs actuall spirit contacts, pacts and bargains?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28439-quelsec","name":"quelsec","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-13T14:35:46-07:00","id":1552337,"title":"","content":"There's no single answer to this.<br /> <br /> A Tradition mage was likely taught a variation of spirit magic where there's a more clear delineation between the two option. Healing with Life will be taught as something like channeling the energy of a powerful spirit that's fundamental to life rather than direct spirit dealings that are accomplished via the Spirit Sphere. An Orphan might be risking turning into a Marauder by not having a meaningful rationalization.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T00:46:02-07:00","id":1552358,"title":"","content":"Remember that everything has a spirit and spirits are everywhere, even if not always active. They also have constant, if uncertain, influence over the world. While Charms represent direct action as represented <b>by the rules</b>, it doesn't really defines the whole of how spirits affect the world.<br /> <br /> So it is perfectly possible for a Mage to assume all their magic is actually the work of spirits. In fact, they may believe that <i><b>everything</b></i> is the work of spirits. And, as any paradigm, <b>they may be right</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T02:14:56-07:00","id":1552360,"title":"","content":"This is also not something that solely crops up for spirit mages.<br /> <br /> It's very simple to construct a Technocratic paradigm that would struggle to differentiate between the broad concept of manipulating the physical rules of reality and manipulating Forces as the underlying Sphere of our current understand that reality is largely determined by how energetic fields interact with each other.<br /> <br /> The only big influence here is - as M20 points out - that paradigms tend to be subject to a utility bias. Long standing and organized groups of mages are going to teach and encourage paradigms that avoid potential stumbling blocks for younger mages developing their individual Focus. Paradigms that can clearly differentiate between conceptual empowerment of an effect and direct manipulation of the source(s) of such power, have greater utility than ones that don't and potentially leave a younger mage confused, struggling to succeed in Seekings, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-14T07:33:02-07:00","id":1552368,"title":"","content":"Also, don't forget that even in a paradigm that exclusively focuses on spirits there are more options than just <i>using or commanding spirits</i> to do things. There is also <i>doing things the way spirits would,</i> or <i>using gifts or bestowments learned from spirits. </i>A shaman might even extend the principles of dealing with spirits to other aspects of reality, for example, they could take the approach that <i>everything has a ban whether it knows it or not</i> and exploit those bans accordingly. That last one isn't much different from how many paradigms work anyways<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't make a shaman with an exclusively spirit focused paradigm because shamans, like almost all mages, deal with everything in the world not just the spiritual. Indeed, I'd say they are less likely to take the stance that everything is spirit and more likely to say that spirits are just another part of the world they deal with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2025-07-15T19:08:42-07:00","id":1552435,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552330-spirit-magic-paradigm-vs-reality?p=1552368#post1552368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, don't forget that even in a paradigm that exclusively focuses on spirits there are more options than just <i>using or commanding spirits</i> to do things. There is also <i>doing things the way spirits would,</i> or <i>using gifts or bestowments learned from spirits. </i>A shaman might even extend the principles of dealing with spirits to other aspects of reality, for example, they could take the approach that <i>everything has a ban whether it knows it or not</i> and exploit those bans accordingly. That last one isn't much different from how many paradigms work anyways<br /> <br /> But I wouldn't make a shaman with an exclusively spirit focused paradigm because shamans, like almost all mages, deal with everything in the world not just the spiritual. Indeed, I'd say they are less likely to take the stance that everything is spirit and more likely to say that spirits are just another part of the world they deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>^This. An Indigenous practitioner of their people's traditional Magick might have knowledge of how to deal with the spirits. But they probably also just...have knowledge of herb-lore or similar forms of traditional medicine. They don't need to ask the spirits to heal, because they KNOW the herbs or methods have medicinal properties. (Indeed, this is why Medicine Work is a distinct Practice from Shamanism, despite many Indigenous traditions using such things; the archetypal &quot;Medicine Man/Woman&quot;, or less charitably the &quot;Witch Doctor&quot;).<br /> <br /> A &quot;home-grown&quot; Magickal tradition, made for everyday use, is usually built on a mixture of &quot;whatever works&quot;, without necessarily needing a Grand Unifying Theory behind it all. The latter is the kind of pedantry that High Ritual Magic users, like the Order of Hermes, concern themselves with.<br /> <br /> <br /> Moreover, even if a Shaman DOES believe that their herb-lore heals because of spirits, they don't need Spirit to use it. They just whisper to the herbs, and thus the spirit inside them, to please do their work. Perhaps making a sacrifice or burning sweet incense/tobacco as pre-thanks to the spirit. They don't need to be able to communicate back and forth, just to <i>talk</i> to it. The spirit will hear the Shaman (or not), and will heal (or not). The Shaman's expertise in Life reflects knowing the right words and names and offerings to make the spirit more likely to comply.<br /> <br /> (Indeed, having dealings with a spirit of Health directly can be a way for the Mage to learn what kind of words and names and offerings the spirits like, directly from them. It works for that particular brand of spirit-taught Shaman MtAs sometimes talks about.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-01-28T06:02:54-08:00","id":1557963,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>quelsec</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1552330-spirit-magic-paradigm-vs-reality#post1552330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A shaman may have a paradigm that all magic comes from spirit pacts. Not all effects are spirits though in reality. A healing life effect can be implemented for example without a spirit and the casting mage only believes it does. But here we have the problem how would said mage rationalise his made believe spirits vs actuall spirit contacts, pacts and bargains?</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that spirits can be created from intense emotions or beliefs, I don't think it's quite that easy to claim their spirits are 'made up.' Especially not if their paradigm started to gain traction.<br /> <br /> The spirit doesn't need to be powerful enough to achieve sentience, as long as it's capable of performing the desired functionality of the spell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29009-darkking","name":"DarkKing","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29009_1.png","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2025"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"639"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}